+  // host growth pause alone does not refuse: parking allocates nothing (the
+  // lane keeps what it holds), and every allocation under a pause takes the
+  // parked lane first (reuseCachedStateWhilePaused,
+  // reuseCachedPagesWhilePaused), as targeted governor passes do. On a 24 GB
+  // machine at long context the pause is on almost always (the 2026-11-10
+  // A/B: every park refused).
